As a low-level character I would wish for the following items:


2 blessed scrolls of charging, so that you can recharge the wand when empty

blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail, gets ac down and gives magic protection,
which is very important later in the game

blessed +2 war hammer named Mjollnir, a good weapon is a must in this game.
Of course you can get it by other means then wishing, but you can also
get killed while trying to obtain one...

blessed +2 pair of speed boots, double speed, very useful

blessed potion of invisibility, gives you intrinsic invisibility, so you 
can avoid all the nasties you don't want to fight (like rust monsters, ochre
jellies and others, dragons however have intrinsic see invisible)

Other items to wish for could include: blessed +2 pair of gauntlets of power
(if your strength is poor... say below 16), blessed ring of conflict (might
save your life when fighting the Wizard, for example), 2 blessed scrolls of
enchant weapon (of course you can get these without wishing, but if you have
lots of wishes...)

You can of course try to get +3 items instead of +2 (or 3 items instead of 2),
but I think if you wish for +2 items, you have a better expectation. I haven't
checked it from the code, though (if someone has, he could correct me if I'm
wrong), and most experienced hackers wish for +3 items. When the wand gets
empty the first time, use a charging scroll to recharge. You cannot recharge
it a second time (it will explode if you try to), but you can still get one
extra wish from the "empty" wand. Keep on zapping and sooner or later you
will get the extra wish.



